  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "\\(2:3=8:x\\). What is \\(x\\)? Calculate: \\(8\\times3\\div2=?\\)",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "12",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(2x=24\\), \\(x=12\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Scale both ratio terms\n\nMultiplying both terms of a ratio by the same nonzero number leaves its quotient unchanged. Since \\(8=2\\times4\\), multiply both terms of \\(2:3\\) by \\(4\\):\n\\[\n2:3=(2\\times4):(3\\times4)=8:12.\n\\]\nTherefore \\(x=12\\), which is nonzero as required for \\(8:x\\).",
